-- an atom map between two molecules: a relabelling of the left molecule's atoms onto the right's,
-- with its inverse, preserving each atom's element. This is mass balance, stated without counting
-- anything: an atom of carbon on the left is an atom of carbon on the right, and every atom is
-- accounted for because the map has an inverse. A reaction record with no such map is not a
-- reaction; Lowe's patent corpus has an unbalanced fraction and machine-generated maps, and the
-- 720,768 duplicates were removed by comparing strings with the mapping stripped.
AtomMap : Mol → Mol → Type 0
AtomMap L R = (f : mol-atoms L → mol-atoms R)
            × (g : mol-atoms R → mol-atoms L)
            × ((x : mol-atoms L) → g (f x) ≡ x)
            × ((y : mol-atoms R) → f (g y) ≡ y)
            × ((x : mol-atoms L) → mol-el R (f x) ≡ mol-el L x)
